{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["The Master, YHWH — and the land is His, so that no man will covet your land when you go up to appear, as is explicit in the pericope of Ki Tissa: ״Three times in the year all your males shall appear before the Master, YHWH, the Elohim of Israel.״ And adjacent to it: ״For I will drive out nations from before you and widen your border, and no man will covet your land when you go up to appear, etc.״ And so in every place, according to the subject of the matter, Scripture calls the Holy One, blessed be He, by [an appellation] appropriate to the pericope. And our Sages too expounded: ״הנה האדון ה׳ צבאות מסעף פארה״ — wherever you find this expression, it means removing one set of tenants and bringing in another set of tenants."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {0 "The parenthetical (בהקב״ה) appears to gloss which divine name is being used in each pericope; translated literally. The Sages' citation is from Isaiah 10:33 with derashic interpretation."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:42:49.501276998Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}